  "text": "Here are three solid picks for a long flight:\n\n1. **\"Project Hail Mary\" by Andy Weir** \u2013 A lone astronaut wakes up with amnesia on a solo mission to save humanity. Fast-paced, funny, and packed with clever problem-solving \u2014 hard to put down.\n\n2. **\"The Martian\" by Andy Weir** \u2013 If you haven't read this one yet, it's the same author's earlier hit: an astronaut stranded on Mars MacGyvering his way to survival. Great tension, light tone, perfect for chunks of reading between distractions.\n\n3. **\"Children of Time\" by Adrian Tchaikovsky** \u2013 A more expansive, thoughtful epic about an uplifted spider civilization and the last remnants of humanity searching for a new home. Longer and richer \u2014 good for a longer haul flight where you want to sink into something meatier.\n\nAll three balance page-turning plots with self-contained arcs, so you're not left hanging if you only get through one."
